# Project specification

The searchable specification is `docs/spec/metro-is-just-a-bus.md` (statement v1.0, 2026-09-29). The original PDF is in `docs/spec/`. An identical copy lives in `metro-web`; when updating the statement, update both.

Permanent agent context (SDD): `.ai/steering/` (`product.md`, `tech-stack.md`, `conventions.md`, `principles.md`) and `AGENTS.md`.

## What to read when

- **Default (implementation):** `.ai/steering/` and `AGENTS.md`. Do not load the full statement only for deadlines or grading.
- **Milestone / delivery / grading / alignment checks:** read `docs/spec/metro-is-just-a-bus.md` (milestones and evaluation criteria). PDF prevails on conflict.
- **Domain or architecture while coding:** steering plus Technical Description / architecture sections of the statement as needed.

Before deciding behavior, component boundaries, or contracts, read steering (and the statement when relevant).

Fixed constraints:

- Distributed system. A single REST backend with all functionality is not enough.
- At minimum: passenger/ops web app, core backend, independently deployable supporting service(s), and notifications across an independent application boundary.
- Synchronous APIs and asynchronous messaging, with failures, retries, and duplicates handled (no repeated ticket, validation, or notification).
- A notification outage must not block network consultation.
